	<h2>Why now</h2>
	<p>
		Search has changed more in the last couple of years than in the previous decade.
		The rise of large language models has given buyers a new way to research —
		asking ChatGPT, Perplexity or Google's AI Overviews a question and getting a
		direct answer, often without ever clicking through to a website. Google AI
		Overviews alone now show up in roughly half of all searches.
	</p>
	<p>
		Some of what worked before still works. Good content, clear structure and a
		credible site still matter — that hasn't changed. What's changed is how that
		content gets found, read and cited. It's no longer just about ranking on a
		results page. It's about being the source an AI system trusts enough to quote.
	</p>
	<p>
		That means the way most companies approach SEO needs updating — not thrown out,
		but rebuilt around how these systems actually work. That's the gap Tatkraft
		exists to close.
	</p>

